7145+ 7DA0              ;58) sends abort command (in order to abort existing command and get unstuck)
7146+ 7DA0              ;send_ftp_command is the main routine that sends command+ string if needed and returns ftp answer code
7147+ 7DA0              ;IN=A=0=command only (eg. "ABORT"). A=1=comamnd+prepared string from INPUT (eg. "STOR filename"), A=2=command+new INPUT
7148+ 7DA0              ;OUT=A=0=NC=sent ok, awaited ftp code returned correctly
7149+ 7DA0              ;A=1=C=c=1=error sending string
7150+ 7DA0              ;A=2=C=c=11=error in module answer (expected answer ">" not returned)
7151+ 7DA0              ;A=3=C=c=4=sent ok, but return code other than expected
